I doubt that NAOs patch will work on a Windows machine.

I would be astonished if this snippet to improve NetHacks random
numbers would work:

--- nethack-3.4.3-orig/src/hacklib.c    2003-12-07 23:39:13.000000000 +0000
+++ nh343-nao/src/hacklib.c     2008-03-18 21:59:21.000000000 +0000
@@ -460,6 +460,14 @@
 void
 setrandom()
 {
+
+  FILE *fptr = NULL;
+  int rnd[2];
+
+  fptr = fopen("/dev/urandom","r");
+  if (fptr) fread((void *)rnd, sizeof(int),1,fptr);
+  fclose(fptr);
+
        /* the types are different enough here that sweeping the
        different
         * routine names into one via #defines is even more confusing
         */

Isn't even /dev/urandom a Linux-only thing?

